{"id":"n1-150","title":"Verb ようがない (〜you ga nai)","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Expresses 'no way to do something,' 'impossible to do'.","longExplanation":"〜ようがない is used to say that there's no way or method to do something, even if you wanted to.","formation":"Verb (masu stem) + ようがない","examples":[{"jp":"電車が混んでいて、動きようがない。","romaji":"Densha ga konde ite, ugoki you ga nai.","en":"The train is so crowded that I can't move.","words":[{"surface":"電車","vocabId":"1443530","reading":"でんしゃ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"混ん","vocabId":"2849867","reading":"こむ","baseForm":"混む"},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"動き","vocabId":"1451180","reading":"うごき"},{"surface":"よう","vocabId":"1546200","reading":"よう"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":"2098290","reading":"ない"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[8,9,10]},{"jp":"彼はとても早く走るので、追いつきようがない。","romaji":"Kare wa totemo hayaku hashiru no de, oitsuki you ga nai.","en":"He runs so fast, there's no way I can catch up.","words":[{"surface":"彼","vocabId":"1483070","reading":"かれ"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"とても","vocabId":null},{"surface":"早く","vocabId":"1400150","reading":"はやく","baseForm":"早い"},{"surface":"走る","vocabId":"1402540","reading":"はしる"},{"surface":"ので","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"追いつき","vocabId":"1588810","reading":"おいつく","baseForm":"追いつく"},{"surface":"よう","vocabId":"1546200","reading":"よう"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":"2098290","reading":"ない"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[8,9,10]},{"jp":"私には理解しようがない。","romaji":"Watashi ni wa rikai shiyou ga nai.","en":"There's no way for me to understand it.","words":[{"surface":"私","vocabId":"1311110","reading":"わたし"},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"理解","vocabId":